    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "How many minutes are there in a micro-century?\n\n(Assume there are $36\\,525$ days in a century.)",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$52.596\\text{ min}$\n\nA micro-century is one millionth of a century.",
      "worked": "The prefix micro- means one millionth.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}1\\text{ micro-century}&=\\frac{36\\,525}{1\\,000\\,000}\\text{ days}\\\\1\\text{ micro-century}&=0.036525\\text{ days}\\\\1\\text{ micro-century}&=0.036525\\times24\\times60\\text{ min}\\\\1\\text{ micro-century}&=52.596\\text{ min}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 32
